# Every replaces= and conflicts= entry in a packages/shared/ PKGBUILD, one per line:
# "<package dir> :: <field>=<entry> :: <reason>". [pocknix-shared] is in every SoC's repo order,
# so the entry acts on every fleet at once, and replaces= uninstalls on -Syu. check.sh fails on
# an entry without a row and on a row whose entry is gone.
pocknix-desktop-kde :: conflicts=pocknix-desktop<0.1.0-27 :: files that pocknix-desktop shipped before the split
pocknix-desktop-kde :: conflicts=pocknix-desktop-plasma<0.1.0-1.1 :: /etc/xdg/kwinrc, which pocknix-desktop-plasma shipped before it moved here
pocknix-desktop-plasma-mobile :: conflicts=pocknix-desktop<0.1.0-27 :: files that pocknix-desktop shipped before the split
pocknix-session :: conflicts=pocknix-desktop<0.1.0-27 :: steamos-session-select lived in pocknix-desktop before the split
pocknix-base-lock :: replaces=mbedtls :: the base renamed mbedtls to mbedtls3 with no conflicts=, so the old copy must go
pocknix-base-lock :: conflicts=mbedtls :: pairs the replaces= so the swap survives file collisions
pocknix-gamepad-calibration :: replaces=python-pyxel :: retires the GPcal app's runtime
pocknix-gamepad-calibration :: conflicts=python-pyxel :: pairs the replaces=
es-de :: conflicts=emulationstation-de :: provides the old name, one ES-DE install at a time
inputplumber :: conflicts=inputplumber :: our build takes the name over ALARM's
wxwidgets-pocknix :: conflicts=wxwidgets-common :: provides ALARM's wxwidgets split in one package
wxwidgets-pocknix :: conflicts=wxwidgets-gtk3 :: provides ALARM's wxwidgets split in one package
pocknix-bsp-common :: conflicts=linux-pocknix-sm8550<7.2.10-3 :: the /flash deploy scripts and hook these kernels shipped (#126)
pocknix-bsp-common :: conflicts=linux-pocknix-sm8250<7.2.10-4 :: the /flash deploy scripts and hook these kernels shipped (#126)
